Tidy the root: bin/ and tests/ into site/, everything written down into docs/, README emptied

> It's our repository to make messy. However, it's too messy for how little is
> going on so far. I wanna be able to show it to someone, and that readme is,
> like, eighteen miles long.

The root, before and after:

| before | after |
|---|---|
| `ADVOCATE.md` `CLAUDE.md` `CONTENT-TODO.md` `DESIGN-NOTES.md` `Gemfile` `MANIFEST.md` `NODE.md` `PAYMENTS-CHECKLIST.md` `README.md` `REDIRECTS.md` `RESERVE-DESIGN.md` `REVIEW-NOTES.md` `STATION.md` `_config.yml` `advocate.yml` `wrangler.jsonc` `api/` `script/` `site/` `site-template/` `tests/` `worker/` | `CLAUDE.md` `Gemfile` `README.md` `_config.yml` `advocate.yml` `wrangler.jsonc` `api/` `docs/` `site/` `site-template/` `worker/` |

Thirteen loose documents became one directory. (`api/` goes in #74.)

## `script/` → `site/bin/`, `tests/` → `site/tests/`

> Script is a lot of stuff for us, but it is support so far for the site itself.
> So I would like to supply those in the site directory. That needs to be some
> kind of bin folder in there instead. Those are tasks that a worker would wanna
> call on, and they just belong in that context. The tests are pretty much the
> same way.

Done, and it reads better up close: a sync that writes `_data/` now sits one
level above the thing it writes, so its paths are `../_data/...` instead of
`../site/_data/...`. Every script's path constants were rewritten rather than
patched — the convention is now `SITE` for the build root and `REPO` for the
node, stated in a comment at the top of each.

**The catch, and what I did about it.** `site/` is the Jekyll source, so
anything in it publishes unless excluded. Two `exclude:` entries bring back a
list that #70 deleted on the grounds that lists are a hazard — so this is not
the same list, and the difference is the point:

- The old one named **eleven documents, one line per file**, and the failure
  mode was the twelfth. Three of them reached a public URL that way; the one
  that mattered was `REVIEW-NOTES.md`, unratified board feedback, verbatim.
- These are **two directories**. Adding a script or a spec needs no edit here,
  so there is nothing to forget.
- And it is now **checked, not trusted**:
  `site/bin/test_nothing_internal_is_published.py` fails if `_site/bin/` or
  `_site/tests/` exists, or if anything ending `.py`, `.spec.js`,
  `package-lock.json` or `playwright.config.js` reaches the output. It runs in
  `smoke.yml` and it has a test asserting that its own guard would catch the
  files it is guarding, because a check that cannot fail proves nothing.

Documents stay outside `source:` — the root or `docs/` — where Jekyll cannot see
them at all. That property is unchanged and is why `docs/` is safe.

## The README is empty

> If you think that there is anything inside the readme that you wanna save,
> I'm gonna suggest you move it to somewhere else, and we're gonna truncate the
> readme so that it's empty.

Zero bytes. **Nothing was deleted** — all seventeen sections of the 68 KB
original are in `docs/`, split by subject and otherwise unchanged apart from
paths:

| | |
|---|---|
| `docs/running-it.md` | the idea, building locally, the tree, adding a page, tests |
| `docs/payments.md` | the five transactions, Stripe, hosted forms, Booqable, forms |
| `docs/identity.md` | members and sign-in, and all of check-in |
| `docs/programming.md` | Cablecast, class mode, featuring things on the homepage |
| `docs/deploying.md` | Cloudflare, and Azure |
| `docs/known-issues.md` | what is wrong and known to be wrong |

I split rather than pruned deliberately. Deciding what to *delete* from 68 KB of
accumulated operational knowledge is a bigger judgment than "move it somewhere
else", and `git log` was never going to be where you look for the Cloudflare
build settings. **If you want it thinned, point at what is dead and that is a
second pass.** The one thing I would not lose from it is the "Path / root
directory `/`" reasoning in `docs/deploying.md`: it is the only written record
of five dashboard fields no agent can read.

`docs/README.md` is the index, and says why the root README is empty and that a
short one comes back when the shape stops moving.

## Verified

- Site builds; output unchanged in shape. **Nothing from `bin/`, `tests/` or
  `docs/` reaches `_site`.**
- All thirteen check suites pass from their new homes — calendar, claim minter,
  tokens, show proposer, catalog report, price list plus `--check`, repricing,
  feed reader, no-secrets, the new publish guard, member-template round trip,
  and the broker's 119 tests.
- **Three real breaks found and fixed on the way**, and the first two were
  invisible to a text search for `script/`:
  1. `worker/test/enroll.test.mjs` resolved `mint-claim.py` through
     `'..', '..', 'script'` — the path was split across quoted segments.
  2. Six `*.spec.js` files defined `REPO` as one level up from `tests/`, which
     is now `site/` and not the repository. Renamed to `SITE_DIR` — and `SITE`
     was already taken in three of them by `'fcpublicmedia/janes-show'`, which
     is why the first rename failed to parse.
  3. **My own sweep corrupted a regex.** `meet.spec.js` had
     `toMatch(/<\s*script/i)` and the rewrite turned it into
     `/<\s*site/bin/i`, which is a syntax error, not a wrong path. Every
     touched `.js`, `.mjs` and `.py` file is now syntax-checked, and that is how
     it was caught.
- The generated `_data/*.json` files carry a `_note` naming the script that
  wrote them; those are updated, still valid JSON, and match what the scripts
  now emit, so the next sync produces no churn.

## Notes

- **`advocate.yml` now points at `docs/ADVOCATE.md`.** The seats' constitution
  moved with everything else; the engine reads a path, so this is the whole
  change.
- **`redirect-report.py` writes `docs/REDIRECTS.md`** now.
- **This is one PR rather than four** because the pieces share their files:
  you cannot move `script/` without rewriting every mention of it, most mentions
  were in the README, and the README is being emptied. Splitting it would have
  meant doing the same reference work twice and resolving the conflict by hand.
- **It does not touch `api/`**, so it and #74 are independent. If #74 lands
  first, one line in `docs/running-it.md`'s tree and one in `docs/NODE.md`'s
  want deleting.

## #75 and this one collide, and the fix is an order

**Merge [#75](../../pull/75) first.** It adds `TENANCY.md` at the root and edits
`NODE.md`, `README.md` and `STATION.md` there; this one moves two of those into
`docs/` and truncates the third to zero bytes. Whichever lands second has to be
resolved by hand, and I would rather it were this one, because relocating files
is what this PR is *for* — so I can take #75's edits, move `TENANCY.md` into
`docs/` with its siblings, and add it to the index, in one rebase.

Merged the other way round, `TENANCY.md` is the one document left loose at a
root that this PR just finished emptying, and somebody has to notice.

Nothing is stacked: this branch is cut from `main` and does not depend on #75.
It is only the order of merging that matters.
